'''Drun Cairnwick'''<ref name="Comic">[[Obi-Wan Kenobi 3|''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' 3]]</ref> was an individual whose name was carved on the wall of the facility used by the [[Hidden Path]] on the [[planet]] [[Jabiim]]. The Path was a network that smuggled [[Force-sensitive]]s and [[Jedi]] away from the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="Part V">{{Kenobi|Part V}}</ref> in [[9 BBY]].<ref name="Timeline">{{KenobiDate|V}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Drun Cairnwick was introduced into the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in "[[Part V]]" of ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'', released on [[June 15]], [[2022]].<ref name="Part V" /> In [[Star Wars Legends|Legends]] continuity, [[Drun Cairnwick/Legends|Drun Cairnwick]] was a [[Jedi Initiate/Legends|Jedi initiate]] who served the [[Jedi Order/Legends|Jedi Order]] and escaped the fall of the Order during the [[Great Jedi Purge/Legends|Great Jedi Purge]]. He was first mentioned in ''[[Galaxy Guide 6: Tramp Freighters]]'', a sourcebook published for ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]'' by [[West End Games]] in [[1990]].<ref name="GG6">''[[Galaxy Guide 6: Tramp Freighters]]''</ref>

